.TH TERMNAV-TMUX-FOCUS 1 "2026-08-25" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termnav-tmux-focus \- publish focus ownership between nested tmux layers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav-tmux-focus watch
.B --tmux-socket
.I socket
.B --client-pid
.I pid
.B --client-tty
.I tty
.RI [ --lease-ms " milliseconds" ]
.RI [ --interval-ms " milliseconds" ]
.br
.B termnav-tmux-focus stop
.B --tmux-socket
.I socket
.B --client-pid
.I pid
.B --client-tty
.I tty
.br
.B termnav-tmux-focus sync
.B --tmux-socket
.I socket
.B --client-pid
.I pid
.B --client-tty
.I tty
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termnav-tmux-focus
lets a tmux configuration highlight only the focused leaf pane across nested
tmux sessions. A focused nested client publishes a leased
.B @termnav_child_focus
option on the exact pane in its immediate parent. Local parents are discovered
from the specified client process. Remote parents are reached through the
per-session socket provided by
.BR termnav-relay (1).
.PP
Each layer knows only its immediate parent. Running the same hooks in every
tmux server therefore supports arbitrary nesting depth without naming hosts,
sessions, processes, or a maximum depth. Separate clients attached to the same
inner session retain independent parent claims.
.PP
The publisher renews only while its client is focused. A matching
.B stop
request reconciles that client's active pane when it is still attached and
releases its parent immediately.
The
.B watch
command restores the client's own pane on focus-in before publishing upward.
Every claim also has a bounded lease, so a killed process, broken SSH
connection, or missed hook eventually fails closed. Publisher and expiry
workers are deduplicated with owner-only runtime locks. No helper is retained
for a direct terminal client with no parent route.
.SH TMUX INTEGRATION
Start
.B watch
from the
.B client-attached
and
.B client-focus-in
hooks. Invoke
.B stop
from
.B client-focus-out
and
.B client-detached.
Invoke the lightweight
.B sync
command after pane, window, or session selection only when the target pane has
a stale
.B @termnav_client_unfocused
marker. This repairs the uncommon case where another attachment changed the
selection while a client was unfocused without adding a process to ordinary
navigation.
Pass
.BR socket_path ,
.BR client_pid ,
and
.B client_tty
from the triggering hook rather than reading session-global environment.
.PP
A focused-leaf predicate can be defined as:
.PP
.nf
#{&&:#{pane_active},#{&&:#{m:*focused*,#{client_flags}},#{==:#{@termnav_child_focus},}}}
.fi
.PP
Use that format in active-border and border-label formats. Those formats have
the client context needed to evaluate the focused flag independently for each
attachment.
.PP
Pane content styles are compiled by tmux without client context and are not
reevaluated when a pane user option changes. Keep
.B window-active-style
literal. If active and inactive pane backgrounds differ, set
.B @termnav_inactive_style
to the inactive style. While a child claim is live or the pane's client is
unfocused, Termnav applies that value as a pane-local
.B window-active-style
override and restores any preexisting override once neither condition remains.
This remains a redraw-time zero-process path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --tmux-socket " socket"
Socket of the tmux server owning the client that triggered the hook.
.TP
.BI --client-pid " pid"
PID of that exact tmux client process.
.TP
.BI --client-tty " tty"
Terminal device of that exact tmux client process.
.TP
.BI --lease-ms " milliseconds"
Crash-cleanup lease. The default is 3500 milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --interval-ms " milliseconds"
Focused-client validation and renewal interval. The default is 1000
milliseconds and must be no more than half the lease.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The publisher completed normally, another publisher already owns the same
client, or the client has no parent route.
.TP
.B 1
A tmux focus or style update failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or an invalid lease relationship.
.SH LIMITATIONS
If the exact same outer pane is displayed by multiple outer clients, the
nested application's pane grid is shared and cannot contain different
background colours for each viewer. Distinct parent panes attaching distinct
clients to one inner tmux session are independent and fully supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR termnav-relay (1),
.BR termnav-tmux-context (1)
